---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "Mortgage Payment in DTI Calculations";
const description =
  "Use the full housing payment in DTI so lender-facing qualification math matches reality. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-06-24";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">DTI housing payment</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Mortgage payment in DTI calculations</h1>
    <p>
      This page is for the buyer whose lender math looks tighter than their own spreadsheet because the underwriting version of the
      housing payment includes more than principal and interest.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="DTI housing-payment review, qualification-math framing, and routing between full-payment composition, affordability, and qualification thresholds."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when your DTI answer depends on the full housing payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when your own payment math looks acceptable but the lender's DTI result comes back tighter.</li>
      <li>If you need the payment structure first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If the next question is whether the payment is safe for your budget, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why lender math feels harsher</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      In real underwriting, the underwriting housing number is usually larger than principal and interest alone. Taxes, insurance,
      HOA, and mortgage insurance push the qualification payment higher than the stripped-down figure many buyers start with.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What front-end DTI asks</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        It isolates the housing burden itself. That means PITI, HOA, and PMI all belong in the lender-facing housing number even
        before other debts are added.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What back-end DTI adds</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        It layers in recurring debt outside the home. That is why a front-end pass while back-end fails is common when a borrower has
        auto loans, student loans, or installment debt that was not part of the housing-only comparison.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The comparison that matters most</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare your principal-and-interest-only estimate with the full housing-payment estimate.</li>
      <li>Then compare front-end DTI with back-end DTI using the same income base.</li>
      <li>Only after that should you interpret whether the loan is tight because of housing cost, non-housing debt, or both.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When to move to a different page</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>If the question is housing-payment composition, move to <a href="/guides/what-is-piti">what is PITI</a>.</li>
      <li>If HOA is the hidden cost, move to <a href="/guides/hoa-fees-and-mortgage-payment">hoa fees and mortgage payment</a>.</li>
      <li>If the question is whether the payment is sustainable, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/home-loan-toolkit/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Your home loan toolkit
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Run the DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Rebuild the full payment</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Check affordability</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-06-24</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
